## Approved escalation and reporting register

Record P1 through P4 triggers, acknowledgment targets, update cadence and the accepted fallback ladder. The playbook's example targets remain proposals until adopted. Document which person can withdraw an exposed service, isolate an endpoint, restrict a privileged identity, authorize a rebuild and accept restoration.

| Duty or external recipient | Applicability rule/contract | Clock start and deadline | Authorized sender/backup | Secure route and fallback | Receipt/evidence reference |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Vendor PSIRT and urgent support | [SET] | [SET] | [PRIVATE] | [VERIFY OFFICIAL ROUTE] | [PRIVATE] |
| CISA / national CSIRT / law enforcement | [SET] | [SET] | [PRIVATE] | [VERIFY OFFICIAL ROUTE] | [PRIVATE] |
| Regulator / agency chain / customer / insurer | [SET EACH SEPARATELY] | [SET] | [PRIVATE] | [PRIVATE] | [PRIVATE] |

Test the primary and backup paths under approved exercise conditions, record acknowledgment times, and update after staffing or provider changes. Do not wait for a weekly publication to report a real critical incident.
